en properly trained are uniquely effective at identifying and combating some forms of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would be specialized in Fae and Beasts as those monsters sounds most 'child attacking'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=928906#post928906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. A group based in the far eastern philosophy, taking elements from some forms of Buddihism and Hinduism. In short, a group that believes in karma and the necessity of a turning wheel of life, death, and rebirth....and by extension hunts those things that can be said to &quot;linger&quot; in one incarnation past their natural lifespan. Vampires, ghosts, sin-eaters, mummies, some types of mages....all must be returned to the cycle if the suffering of this world is to be reduced.<br /> <br /> 4. A group of &quot;projectors&quot; that hunt in dreams and Twilight, taking the fight to the ephermeral, driving off things that stalk nightmares, and stalking physical entities from the safety of the unseen realm or deep within their subconscious minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are really cool also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T15:49:40-07:00","id":928923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=928906#post928906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. A group of &amp;quot;redeemed&amp;quot; monsters who have somehow been &amp;quot;cured&amp;quot; of their existence and restored to humanity. The process is grueling, and affects their memories of their time among the damned (or whatever) and the specifics involved in their &amp;quot;cure&amp;quot;. Despite this, most are unwilling to return to their original state- which is why they are willing to work for the organization and bring in more subjects to be cured. Cause whatever the process is, it is temporary and requires &amp;quot;upkeep&amp;quot; every few months. In other words, the organization can effectively demand whatever they want if the beneficiaries of their treatment expect to retain this new found humanity.<br /> <br /> 2. Taking a page from Steven King's It, a conspiracy utilizing children, who when properly trained are uniquely effective at identifying and combating some forms of monster. <br /> <br /> 3. A group based in the far eastern philosophy, taking elements from some forms of Buddihism and Hinduism. In short, a group that believes in karma and the necessity of a turning wheel of life, death, and rebirth....and by extension hunts those things that can be said to &amp;quot;linger&amp;quot; in one incarnation past their natural lifespan. Vampires, ghosts, sin-eaters, mummies, some types of mages....all must be returned to the cycle if the suffering of this world is to be reduced. <br /> <br /> 4. A group of &amp;quot;projectors&amp;quot; that hunt in dreams and Twilight, taking the fight to the ephermeral, driving off things that stalk nightmares, and stalking physical entities from the safety of the unseen realm or deep within their subconscious minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>2 and 4 together are the Merrick Institute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:55:59-07:00","id":929086,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I'm a bit too far behind the times here. What's the Merrick Institute?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T01:52:21-07:00","id":929119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=929086#post929086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I'm a bit too far behind the times here. What's the Merrick Institute?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/892270-conspiracy-the-merrick-institute\">A homebrew.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T02:04:56-07:00","id":929120,"title":"","content":"it's not an homebrew- this is the conspiracy which would show up in the up coming Mortal Remains supplement for Beast shared by David in the forums for review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:19:49-07:00","id":929379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=929120#post929120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not an homebrew- this is the conspiracy which would show up in the up coming Mortal Remains supplement for Beast shared by David in the forums for review.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, looks like I need to learn how to read good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T21:55:14-07:00","id":929553,"title":"","content":"I had an idea that I'm still vacillating between tweaking enough to be usable or abandoning of a group of transhumanists/futurists who started out focusing on dealing with &quot;x-risks&quot; (risks that could potentially endanger humanity as we know it) without knowing of the existence of the supernatural, only to find out about it and repurpose their discoveries to deal with it. They'd have a lot in common RE pragmatism with the CDC/FEMA compact mentioned earlier. <br /> <br /> If they have an Endowment, it'd be various anti-xrisk technology repurposed to deal with the supernatural. Like anti-nanobot &quot;blue goo&quot; that turns out to be effective against Hosts or vampires in mist form, radiation shielding that can also block forms of supernatural energy, memetic hazard inoculation that can undo supernatural brainwashing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:08:12-07:00","id":929595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=929553#post929553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea that I'm still vacillating between tweaking enough to be usable or abandoning of a group of transhumanists/futurists who started out focusing on dealing with &amp;quot;x-risks&amp;quot; (risks that could potentially endanger humanity as we know it) without knowing of the existence of the supernatural, only to find out about it and repurpose their discoveries to deal with it. They'd have a lot in common RE pragmatism with the CDC/FEMA compact mentioned earlier. <br /> <br /> If they have an Endowment, it'd be various anti-xrisk technology repurposed to deal with the supernatural. Like anti-nanobot &amp;quot;blue goo&amp;quot; that turns out to be effective against Hosts or vampires in mist form, radiation shielding that can also block forms of supernatural energy, memetic hazard inoculation that can undo supernatural brainwashing...</div> </div> </div> </div>What if, rather than awesome weapons, your x-risks group instead focuses on increasingly implausible survivability? Serums that render vampire blood less compelling and toxic, an implant that lessens the damage from ephemeral attacks, anti-mesmerism contact lenses, all the way up to mythical digital immortality (so as to survive an apocalyptic event that wipes out civilization).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:15:39-07:00","id":929679,"title":"","content":"That's a good idea, and I might fold that in. I don't really think of them as &quot;awesome weapons&quot;- as is normal for Endowments, very few of them are actually weapons. Of the examples I listed, all of them are defensive in nature and only one of them actually has potential to be used as a weapon. The last two even fit your idea- the armor plating was designed in the 60s for bunkers and the memetic inoculation is completely defensive. But those other ideas are really good. I like the idea that none of their gear was initially designed to protect against the supernatural. Maybe the larger organization's leadership and R&amp;D doesn't acknowledge the supernatural or the danger it poses, and the Conspiracy part is a smaller part of the group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T17:56:48-07:00","id":930622,"title":"","content":"So while researching for my &quot;Mummies in Paris&quot; game I came across the Affair of the poisons and this little gem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chambre_Ardente\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Parlement_de_Normandie_Rouen_2009_13.jpg/960px-Parlement_de_Normandie_Rouen_2009_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chambre_Ardente\" target=\"_blank\"> Chambre Ardente - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chambre_Ardente\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chambre_Ardente </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If my brain is like a sponge and ideas are water, I am currently bone dry right now. Squeezed all my good ideas out on Mummy: The Cursed. But I know this can be something cool. Just no energy to make it. Do me proud, my fellow Hunters (...Vigilantes?) and turn it into something awesome. Best I can do is a French version of the Maleficarium with a little Valkyrie thrown in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:38:50-07:00","id":932387,"title":"","content":"For inspiration for the CDC compact, I'd highly recommend The Strain, since it's about a CDC employee (and eventually an entire Hunter cell) dealing with a viral vampire outbreak. <br /> <br /> I like the idea that the compact initially thought that things like vampirism and lycanthropy were viruses, and has only recently made serious efforts at supernatural outreach, now that they have enough information to know that a lot of the &quot;player splats&quot; are fighting the same things they are, and they don't really have a chance doing it without working with them to some degree. That would be an interesting hook- how did the organization find out? How did the leadership finally conclude that vampirism wasn't viral and that vampires actually attempt to prevent disease outbreaks whenever possible? <br /> <br /> Cognitohazards, memetohazards, and LRDs (localized reality distortions) are also part of what they deal with (since they often exhibit similar qualities to viruses and share the trait of being major threats to humanity as a whole. See the &quot;zombies&quot; from the movie Pontypool for an example. And a certain plot element/flimsy boob excuse from MGSV which may have been based on them), though these are poorly understood and they're only recently developing formalized protocols for dealing with them. Some of the members have also picked up the term &quot;x-risk&quot; from transhumanist and futurist communities, and have started using it to describe their targets instead of just &quot;magic diseases and parasites&quot;.<br /> <br /> They're currently dealing with a need for competent personnel who can handle the more action-y side of things. They try to get ex-military or ex-law enforcement personnel when they can, but due to TFV's headhunting of those areas they often just recruit emergency personnel of various kinds and send them to the shooting range and tell them to focus on learning how to make headshots. <br /> <br /> They can get a fair bit of funding and support when they need it, because they deal with threats that most people (and government agencies) understand and fear. Vampires and werewolves don't really scare most people, but &quot;biohazard&quot; and &quot;radiation&quot; do. They say a clipboard and a lab coat can get you anywhere. A hazmat suit is even better- and most people do whatever someone in a hazmat suit tells them.<br /> <br /> Also, to the directly above poster: you don't always need an entirely new Conspiracy. You could simply have the Chambre operated by France's branch of the Malleus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-16-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T07:00:59-07:00","id":932888,"title":"","content":"Not really serious, but I'm imagining something like frat boys who have no idea what they're doing, but they're having a blast. Two parts Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, one part Ashwood Abbey, called something like the Sons of Broseidon. They get themselves absolutely hammered on some homebrewed booze and offer themselves to a vampire. The vampire takes a bite, get affected by the booze somehow (it's really strong stuff), gets dragged off, staked and tied to the roof of the frat house waiting for the sun to rise.<br /> <br /> Or they throw a kegger at a place sacred to Werewolves. When the woofs show up to object the frat boys start chasing them in their trucks. All that chrome decoration on the bumpers and such? That ain't chrome. It's silver.<br /> <br /> Or they run into a possessed person whom they tie down and essentially waterboard with beer until the spirit leaves. Which somehow works. They are also somehow immune to Disquiet and the radius of the Wasteland is reduced, but only after consuming enough booze. These hunters refer to the created as &quot;Brometheans&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are lead by a bro shrouded in legend and mystery. Only whispers refer to the legendary Broseidon, who lives somewhere on the coast of Californea where he in tune with the ocean and stuff which grants him the deepest of wisdoms. The only ones who have ever spoken to him are Brad and Charlie Renolds-Handelsen. They travel the west coast to visit the chapter houses of the Sons of Broseidon to convey the wisdom of Broseidon and attend the best parties. There's something odd about them though: Brad and Charlie look like they're in their mid-twenties and have done so for at least the last two decades. They are currently engage in the most epic game of gay chicken the country's ever seen: so far they've been happily married for almost five years.<br /> <br /> The Sons of Broseidon have made some progress here and there, but because of their fratboy antics are not as effective as they could be if they got their act together. They share a few institutes of education with the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, who see the Sons as an unruly bunch of losers while the Sons see them as uptight creepy wiccan chicks who need to relax for a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:17:35-07:00","id":939278,"title":"","content":"There isn't really a martial artist conspiracy, and the &quot;warrior monk&quot; one is entirely steeped in Catholicism, so I think there's definitely room there. You could do something based on the first two parts of JJBA, with the Ripple as their Endowment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:50:29-07:00","id":939295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=939278#post939278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really a martial artist conspiracy, and the &amp;quot;warrior monk&amp;quot; one is entirely steeped in Catholicism, so I think there's definitely room there. You could do something based on the first two parts of JJBA, with the Ripple as their Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Conspiracy, but I have an antagonist Mummy cult that's a corrupted Shaolin monastery that preach a doctrine that speaks to the power of instinct and muscle memory over the conscious mind. They slip into disciplined thoughtless berserker rages and effortlessly flow from form to form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:56:19-07:00","id":956630,"title":"","content":"While the upcoming Merrick Institute touches on this somewhat, I think there's room for at least a few groups that focus on the Astral, whether as those who fight Beasts/Changelings/Mind mages/goetia/etc or just those who want to explore the universal subconsciousness. There might even be room somewhere for either a Conspiracy or a Minor Template who aim to bring their ideal Astral forms into reality to replace their current physical bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:08:15-07:00","id":956931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=956630#post956630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the upcoming Merrick Institute touches on this somewhat, I think there's room for at least a few groups that focus on the Astral, whether as those who fight Beasts/Changelings/Mind mages/goetia/etc or just those who want to explore the universal subconsciousness. There might even be room somewhere for either a Conspiracy or a Minor Template who aim to bring their ideal Astral forms into reality to replace their current physical bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got general thoughts for a group that uses their personal Goetia for similar things (Influence \u2022 to augment actions, etc., up to Claim/merging with their own mental facets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:05:01-07:00","id":957030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=930622#post930622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my brain is like a sponge and ideas are water, I am currently bone dry right now. Squeezed all my good ideas out on Mummy: The Cursed. But I know this can be something cool. Just no energy to make it. Do me proud, my fellow Hunters (...Vigilantes?) and turn it into something awesome. Best I can do is a French version of the Maleficarium with a little Valkyrie thrown in.</div> </div> </div> </div>A logical option would be carrying out secret trials of supernaturals. In absentia, or do they capture them first? A room from which outside light is excluded implies secrecy, which might imply they respect the right of supernaturals judged innocent to remain secret. Of course a room lit by torches implies ready access to fire, which is a habitual monster-killing tool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of things not covered by canon, we haven't seen much in the way of super-humanities. A conspiracy that discovered a profound insight into human nature, allowing psychological and sociological models to be predictive to a &quot;super&quot; degree. IIRC there was some work done on a Chinese governmental conspiracy that was something like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 08-24-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:04:47-07:00","id":957932,"title":"","content":"I once wrote up a secret division of the Georgia Historical Society as a compact dedicated to learning the supernatural truth behind the history of Georgia in general and Savannah's occult stuffed history in particular. They generally didn't kill monsters unless said monster became a threat to either their members, a Georgia historic site, or the tourist revenue resulting from said history and were allied with another compact in Savannah that was a ghost tour company that worked with the monsters to drive up ticket sales by pushing the limits of the masquerade in plausibly deniable ways.<br /> <br /> they were the sorts of guys that would literally interview vampires to learn how the supposed &quot;masonic autopsies&quot; that went on in the tunnel beneath Savannah to find a cure for yellow fever in the 1800s were the of the ordo pretending to be masons.<br /> <br /> I think similar compacts of historians studying the secret history (as opposed to the more Indiana Jones style Aegis Kai Doru) could work in other areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:22:31-07:00","id":961829,"title":"","content":"Has their been an analogue to the dresden files Paranet? Minor mystics with just a supernatural merit rather than a full blown template. With there being 15+ merits in the CofD core seems like it would be a thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:37:56-07:00","id":961841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914510-what-niches-haven-t-been-covered-by-canon-organizations?p=961829#post961829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has their been an analogue to the dresden files Paranet? Minor mystics with just a supernatural merit rather than a full blown template. With there being 15+ merits in the CofD core seems like it would be a thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Those merits largely came from an awesome 1e book called Second Sightbthat detailed psychics and gedge wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:02:08-07:00","id":962486,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this has been mentioned yet (haven't had a chance to really dig through the thread yet), but I had bounced around the idea of a Prometheus-hunting sect born out of Rabbinic society. It's comprised of a group of scholars who research the nature and motives of golems and the cadre of enforcers that are whispered about in rumor but can be tracked down when a neighborhood is being terrorized by something that should not be. I figure their focus is promethei, but they probably have their fair share of knowledge on the restless dead (both ghosts and vampires) as well.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of an organized crime focused compact that someone mentioned on the first page, but I'd probably focus on something local rather than global. Picture Chicago in the 1920s. An upstart Sicilian by the name of Alfredo Giovanni is aggressively encroaching on the territory of the local crime bosses. He has no respect for the traditions and courtesies of the established law, and while his forces are small, they're incredibly aggressive and fanatically loyal. The local families are losing soldiers, goods, and territory at alarming rates, and they eventually arrange a sit-down to address the problem. Their solution is a temporary armistice. They assign some of their best capos to serve as a spear against the Giovanni invasion, and after years of fighting, Giovanni's head finally ends up on a pike. But the men who led the charge are changed. They've seen the horror that lives in the shadows, and they decide to form their own family. For decades now, they've persisted as a substrata of Chicago's underworld. Any crime lord who's anybody pays them their monthly tithes, and while many cry that it's extortion, few will actually miss a payment. Their agenda is purely territorial. They keep the interests of the existing families free of the supernatural, and in return, they get a bite out of everybody's slice of the pie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-02-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}